# dotfiles-nvim/.gitignore — this repo is editor config only; never machine state.
*.log
*.bak
.DS_Store

# NOT nvim/lazy-lock.json. It is the POINT of this repo — the committed plugin pins every
# consumer resolves against, moved only by scripts/update-nvim-plugins.sh under review.
# A blanket `*lock*` rule would hide it, which is why there is not one.

# lazy.nvim writes its working lockfile into $XDG_STATE_HOME, never into the config tree
# (#465), so nothing under nvim/ should ever appear untracked. If something does, that is
# a finding — do not add a rule here to make it quiet.

# The gate's throwaway sandboxes live under $TMPDIR and are removed by the dispatchers'
# EXIT traps; nothing lands in the checkout.
